    {"id":"concept_referral_lifecycle_state_machine","label":"12-State Referral Lifecycle State Machine","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/hassanabdelmenem/antigravity/eha-transfer/.agents/explorer_m4_3/handoff.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"The referral transfer process is modeled as an explicit 12-value status enum (pending, dept_approved, manager_approved, accepted, patient_consented, rejected, in_transit, arrived, admitted, discharged, postponed, cancelled) so that every clinical handoff step across facilities, roles, and consent gates is individually auditable and independently securable."},
    {"id":"concept_valid_status_transition_graph","label":"Valid Status Transition Graph & Actor Permissions","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/hassanabdelmenem/antigravity/eha-transfer/.agents/explorer_m4_3/handoff.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"validStatusTransition() and transitionActorAllowed() in firestore.rules mirror the client-side mutation guards exactly, so that no illegal state jump or off-party write can bypass DataContext.tsx by writing directly to Firestore."},
    {"id":"concept_bed_capacity_race_condition","label":"Debounced Bed Stepper Race Condition & Whole-Map Clobber Risk","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/hassanabdelmenem/antigravity/eha-transfer/.agents/explorer_m5_1/handoff.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"BedManagementPage debounces stepper taps 500ms per bed type but updateFacilityCapacity spreads the entire capacity map on write; concurrent edits to different bed types, snapshot reseeds mid-tap, and unmounts within the debounce window can silently drop or clobber occupancy changes. Recommended fix: atomic per-bed-type dot-path Firestore updates plus a pending-writes ref flushed on unmount."},
    {"id":"concept_direct_admission_workflow","label":"Direct (Walk-In) Patient Admission Workflow","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/hassanabdelmenem/antigravity/eha-transfer/.agents/explorer_m5_2/handoff.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Walk-in patients bypass the multi-facility referral pipeline entirely via a separate directAdmissions collection and addDirectAdmission mutation that atomically increments bed occupancy, letting nursing staff admit ER walk-ins without creating a cross-facility referral record."},
    {"id":"concept_accompanying_doctor_guard","label":"Accompanying Doctor Escort Guard Before Dispatch","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/hassanabdelmenem/antigravity/eha-transfer/.agents/explorer_m4_3/handoff.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"When requiresAccompanyingDoctor is set on a referral, both DataContext.tsx and firestore.rules block the in_transit transition until an escort doctor's name and phone number are recorded, ensuring a clinician physically accompanies the patient during ambulance transport."},
    {"id":"concept_audit_trail_append_only","label":"Append-Only Audit Trail Invariant (statusHistory)","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/hassanabdelmenem/antigravity/eha-transfer/.agents/explorer_m4_3/handoff.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"auditTrailAppendOnly() in firestore.rules restricts statusHistory array growth to 0 or 1 entries per write and pins the first entry, preventing retroactive falsification of the clinical/administrative audit record."},
    {"id":"concept_rbac_14_role_taxonomy","label":"14-Role RBAC Taxonomy Across 6 Personas","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/hassanabdelmenem/antigravity/eha-transfer/.agents/explorer_survey_1/report.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"14 distinct roles are grouped into 6 operational personas (referring clinician, HoD, medical director/manager, ER official, nursing staff, system admin) so that UI capability gating and Firestore rule predicates can be defined once per persona rather than per individual role."},
    {"id":"concept_sla_breach_escalation","label":"30-Minute SLA Breach Auto-Escalation","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/hassanabdelmenem/antigravity/eha-transfer/.agents/explorer_survey_1/report.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Client-side sweeps duplicate scheduled Cloud Functions SLA checks (src/lib/sla.ts, functions/src/sla.ts) so time-critical escalation still fires even on the Firebase Spark (free) plan where always-on server-side schedulers are constrained."},
    {"id":"concept_offline_sync_architecture","label":"Offline Draft Persistence & IndexedDB Sync","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/hassanabdelmenem/antigravity/eha-transfer/.agents/explorer_survey_1/report.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Form drafts persist to localStorage and offline referral submissions queue in IndexedDB (idb) so referring clinicians in low-connectivity facilities do not lose intake data; offlineSync.ts auto-syncs queued referrals on reconnect."},
    {"id":"concept_e2e_dom_selector_contracts","label":"Bed Management E2E/DOM Selector Contracts","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/hassanabdelmenem/antigravity/eha-transfer/.agents/explorer_m5_3/handoff.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Playwright and Vitest suites hard-code exact headings, aria-labels, and text patterns (e.g. '/Bulk Bed Management/i', 'free of {total}', '/Admit to (ICU|CCU|PICU|Ward) bed/i'); any Milestone 5 refactor must preserve these verbatim to avoid breaking the 568-test baseline."},
    {"id":"concept_capacity_hub_unification","label":"Unified Bed Capacity & Admission Control Center","file_type":"concept","source_file":"/Users/hassanabdelmenem/antigravity/eha-transfer/.agents/explorer_m5_2/handoff.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Milestone 5 merges bed capacity steppers, the arrived-transfer quick-admit queue, and walk-in direct admission into a single BedManagementPage hub via an embedded modal, so nursing staff no longer navigate away to /admissions/new mid-workflow, while that route is retained as a thin wrapper for 100% backwards compatibility."}
  ],
